  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\frac{\\sin ^4 x}{2}+\\frac{\\cos ^4 x}{3}=\\frac{1}{5}$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CIW4z",
      "text": "\n$\\tan ^2 x=\\frac{2}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "IkLHt",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\sin ^8 x}{8}+\\frac{\\cos ^8 x}{27}=\\frac{1}{125}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "0KV5q",
      "text": "\n$\\tan ^2 x=\\frac{1}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DlrYv",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\sin ^8 x}{8}+\\frac{\\cos ^8 x}{27}=\\frac{2}{125}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\sin ^4 x}{2}+\\frac{\\cos ^4 x}{3}=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{\\sin ^4 x}{2}+\\frac{\\left(1-\\sin ^2 x\\right)^2}{3}=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\sin ^4 x}{2}+\\frac{1+\\sin ^4 x-2 \\sin ^2 x}{3}=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad 5 \\sin ^4 x-4 \\sin ^2 x+2=\\frac{6}{5} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad 25 \\sin ^4 x-20 \\sin ^2 x+4=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad\\left(5 \\sin ^2 x-2\\right)^2=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\sin ^2 x=\\frac{2}{5}, \\cos ^2 x=\\frac{3}{5}, \\tan ^2 x=\\frac{2}{3} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad \\frac{\\sin ^8 x}{8}+\\frac{\\cos ^8 x}{27}=\\frac{1}{125} \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
